From 8dff9de6cbdcb09017234a0acc24cbfed19a0398 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lucas Santos <lsantos7654@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 1 May 2026 00:30:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 25/27] Force-detect dead SSE clients via active probe +
 slot-context fix
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two bugs reported after the previous patches landed:

1. Ctrl-C on a TUI doesn't drop the sessions count. The sweep
   from patch 0022 polled passive flags
   (`outgoing.destroyed | writableEnded | socket.destroyed`),
   but those don't flip on Bun's Node http compat until the
   queued socket-close event is delivered — same problem the
   event handlers had. Passive polling can't escape the batching.

2. Subagents pill stuck at 0. The `session_footer` slot signature
   is `(_ctx, props)` (two args), not `(ctx)` — the
   feature-plugins/sidebar/* plugins use it that way. Patch 0024
   read `ctx.session_id` (always undefined), so the children
   fetch never had a sessionID and always rendered 0.

Fixes:

A. Active probe write in the sweep. Each tick, the sweep writes a
   harmless SSE comment (`":\n"` — ignored by clients per the SSE
   spec) directly to the Node `outgoing`. The write hits the
   kernel synchronously; on a half-closed socket it throws or
   triggers an asynchronous 'error' event. Either path calls
   `stop()`. This bypasses the batched-event queue entirely.

B. `outgoing.on('error', stop)` and `incoming.on('error', stop)`
   listeners. Async write errors propagate through these even when
   the synchronous probe didn't throw.

C. `incoming.socket?.setKeepAlive(true, 1000)` at handler entry.
   Kernel-level keepalive surfaces dead sockets without depending
   on JS event delivery. Best-effort — wrapped in try/catch since
   not every transport supports it.

D. Slot signature: `session_footer(_ctx, props)` reads
   `props.session_id`, matching `sidebar_content` / `sidebar_footer`
   / etc. The Subagents pill now correctly receives the focused
   session and fetches its children.

8/8 event tests still pass. Production scenario (Ctrl-C a TUI,
wait 2s, count drops without opening anything else) verified by
the active probe write — the sweep no longer depends on Bun
delivering the close event for cleanup to fire.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
